# Tailwind CSS Styling Guidelines

This project uses Tailwind CSS v4 for styling with a custom CSS variable-based theming system.

## CSS Configuration

The project uses **[globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)** which includes:
- Tailwind CSS import via `@import "tailwindcss"`
- CSS variables for theming (`--background`, `--foreground`)
- Dark mode support via `prefers-color-scheme`
- Custom font variables from Geist fonts

## Styling Conventions

### 1. Use Tailwind Classes First
- Prefer Tailwind utility classes over custom CSS
- Use responsive prefixes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`
- Use state modifiers: `hover:`, `focus:`, `active:`, `disabled:`

### 2. CSS Variables for Theming
Current CSS variables available:
- `--background` / `--color-background`
- `--foreground` / `--color-foreground` 
- `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-sans`
- `--font-geist-mono` / `--font-mono`

### 3. Dark Mode Implementation
- Use CSS variables that automatically switch based on `prefers-color-scheme`
- Apply `dark:` prefix classes when needed for specific dark mode styles
- Example: `bg-background text-foreground` uses the CSS variables

### 4. Component Styling Patterns

**Flashcard Components:**
```tsx
// Card container
className="bg-white dark:bg-black border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-lg p-6"

// Interactive elements
className="hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-900 transition-colors"

// Text hierarchy
className="text-3xl font-semibold text-foreground"
className="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"
```

### 5. Layout Patterns
- Use flexbox and grid utilities: `flex`, `grid`, `items-center`, `justify-between`
- Responsive spacing: `p-4 md:p-6 lg:p-8`
- Container patterns: `max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4`

### 6. Best Practices
- Group related classes logically (layout, spacing, colors, typography)
- Use consistent spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32...)
- Leverage Tailwind's design tokens for consistency
- Use `clsx` or `cn` utility for conditional classes when needed with shadcn/ui